  "text": "Nurek grew from 74.3 to 89.7 km² (+21%) between 2026-06-27 and 2026-10-13. Rogun grew from 13.9 to 20.0 km² (+44%), water level ≈ 1115 → 1128 m (DEM estimate, ±10 m). Both seen on the same NISAR passes, so the numbers are directly comparable.",
  "interpretation": "Both reservoirs filled during summer 2026. Nurek's seasonal refill: +15.4 km2 of new water, almost all of it along the shallow edges of the lake. Rogun: the new reservoir pushed about 8 km2 of new water up the Vakhsh valley (cyan), and the estimated level rose about 13 m, mostly between mid-August and early September. The small orange patches (2.1 km2) are at the far upstream end, in the river channel above the reservoir: in late June the river was wide with snow- and glacier-melt water, by October it is narrower. This is the river, not the reservoir shrinking.",
